%description:

Tcp.initialSendSequenceNumber:invalid -- a value below -1 stops the run with an error.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "-1: from the clock"; the code accepts -1 and 0 to 4294967295
(TcpConnection::selectInitialSeqNum()).

The classes: clock (-1, the default), fixed (a value from 0 to 4294967295), random (a
distribution, which the parameter takes again for each connection, because it is volatile),
invalid (below -1 or above 4294967295). The code: TcpConnection::selectInitialSeqNum().

Host under test: host1, whose connection selects its ISS at the open. Observation: the error,
and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.initialSendSequenceNumber
%# class: invalid
%# value: -2
%# key: *.host1.tcp.initialSendSequenceNumber
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpInitialSendSequenceNumberInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.initialSendSequenceNumber = -2    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
initialSendSequenceNumber must be -1 or 0 to 4294967295, but it is -2
